      "desc:8": "The Singularity Drilling Hub is a 12x12x12 steel cube that drives worker nodes across chunks: miner nodes dig ores, drilling nodes pull underground fluids — everything lands in the hub's own buses and hatches. Its controller recipe bills 16 singularities; binding a worker costs 1 more.\n\nThe steam bill scales with headcount: 8,000 L/s of superheated base plus each active node's tier cost — drillers 2K/6K/12K/20K, miners 5K/10K/20K/80K/240K by tier. Idle nodes cost nothing, and the hub gets no 4x speedup from superheated — it simply demands it.\n\nGrow the network node by node: one miner first, then a driller, then upgrades. Bound nodes chunk-load themselves and their work area.",
